## Outcome and conditions

Derive joint welfare/cost accounting and interpret local activity, abatement and defence margins with model limits. Required components: actor_and_cost_accounting, three_marginal_conditions, curvature_and_behavioural_boundaries. Supported work may use the cited notes; independent checks use no notes, internet, solution or hints. A basic calculator and blank paper are allowed; reasoning, formula selection and assumptions must be supplied by the learner. Numerical examples below are agent-created hypothetical instantiations unless explicitly labelled as a finished-note example. They do not assert current market or policy facts.

[[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Economics_of_Green_Deal/Week_2/Road_Transport_External_Costs.md#Activity abatement and defence are jointly chosen|Activity abatement and defence are jointly chosen]]
[[01_Notes/2026_2027/Winter_Semester/Economics_of_Green_Deal/Week_2/Road_Transport_External_Costs.md#Assumptions and derivative notation|Assumptions and derivative notation]]
